From 3ffae9fdecf2c467334235e81725e443d5b5318b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 02:28:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/30] Recover rbbr_sender_utilizing_rwnd and sanitize
 bounds-safety types

- rbbr_sender_utilizing_rwnd: take the RTT median (sorted samples,
  falling back to median_rtt), derive the expected bytes from
  win * measure_ms / median, compute utilization from
  cycle_bytes_rcvd, and report low utilization through tcp_log_bbr
  with the reference format string and line 825.
- Sanitize 11 compiler-internal __bounds_safety type names into real C
  types with __counted_by/__sized_by annotations (u_char *, void *,
  uint32_t *, bitmap_t *, struct inpcb **).
- Declare tcp_log_bbr in tcp_log.h.

Remaining explicit stubs: 301.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
